  "text": "One tooth gives a crocodile away. This is an alligator. This is a crocodile. How are they different? Alligators have broader, U-shaped snouts. Crocodiles usually have narrower, V-shaped snouts. With its mouth shut, a crocodile's fourth lower tooth still sticks out. An alligator hides its lower teeth. This is a turtle. This is a tortoise. So how do you tell them apart? Turtles often live in water. Tortoises are land-dwellers. A sea turtle can swim 22 miles an hour. A giant tortoise? Under half a mile an hour. At the zoo, I just look for that one tooth. Follow so you learn something new every day!",
